## Test Coverage Summary (for review purposes)

The integration test at `live-claude-smoke-test.integration.test.ts` validates
all 10 acceptance criteria from `docs/specs/live-claude-smoke-test.md`:

- AC #1 — exactly one live test case in the file
- AC #2 — real `claude` binary spawned with production flag set; imports
  `AGENT_ALLOWED_TOOLS` from `src/orchestrator/agents.ts` (no duplication)
- AC #3 — no `jest.mock("child_process", ...)`, no `spawn`/`execFile` stubs
- AC #4 — cheap "say ok" prompt; no `--system-prompt`; no tool use; no project
  tree writes; no extra network calls beyond `claude --print`
- AC #5 — pass requires: exit code 0, non-empty trimmed stdout, no stdin-warning
  match in either stream, no permission-denied match in either stream
- AC #6 — fail message includes redacted argv, exit code, truncated (≤ 2000
  chars) stdout and stderr — diagnosable from CI logs alone
- AC #7 — skips (not fails) on `RAPTOR_SKIP_LIVE_CLAUDE` truthy OR `claude`
  missing from PATH; per-skip reason logged via `console.log`
- AC #8 — per-test timeout 60000 ms set on the `it(...)` call; no global
  `jest.setTimeout` mutation
- AC #9 — picked up by both `npm test` and `npm run test:integration` via the
  existing `testMatch` glob; no new script
- AC #10 — top-of-file comment documents (a) why the file is non-mocked,
  (b) the PR #13 stdin and Hotfix `95a1a62` permission regressions, and
  (c) the AC #7 skip rules

